# cpp slice: the committed crossing counts of the D18 core grid (CAMPAIGN section 4.0), full build: one row per timed
# core-ffi row of the grid (both gates compare every '  P'/'  U' row: wp5_gate.sh and run_campaign.sh --suite gate).
# Taken 2026-10-03 with counts_grid (links the rpc,count campaign core): the transport-ready encode (end state (ii)):
# encode_into_* + ak_enc_take_owned + ak_bytes_free (take = those two, from the core's RPC counters), and the decode
# from the contiguous buffer (decode_with_*_unk, one reset); the 16 shapes in ASCII (P7.1 decode only), P2.2 Latin-1 and wide, the 7 U-* rows.
# New rows against counts-baseline.log: every 'encode ... transport' row (24), the P2.2/latin1 and P2.2/wide decode rows and P7.1's
# decode (counted nowhere before); the other decode rows
# equal counts-baseline's (decode retain / decode) for the same payload. Deterministic.
counting build (D18 core grid), linkage=shared, -std=201703
One row per timed core-ffi row of CAMPAIGN 4.0's grid. forward = core + host + take: host = ak_enc_reset
(encode) and the one ak_dec_reset_<Root> of a retain decode; take = ak_enc_take_owned + ak_bytes_free
(the transport-ready encode), from the core's RPC counters.

